          "label": "<p>After caring for a patient on contact precautions, a nurse begins removing her P</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>After caring for a patient on contact precautions, a nurse begins removing her PPE. What is the correct doffing order?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Mask → gown → eye protection → gloves</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>This order is reversed. Gloves are the most contaminated item and must come off first; the mask is removed last because its ties are the least contaminated surface.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Gown → gloves → mask → eye protection</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>The gown is removed third, not first. Starting with gloves is essential because their outer surface carries the heaviest contamination from direct patient contact.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Gloves → eye protection → gown → mask</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct! Gloves come off first (highest contamination), followed by hand hygiene, then eye protection (by ear pieces only), gown (rolled inside-out), and mask last (by ties or loops). Hand hygiene is performed again after the mask.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Eye protection → gown → gloves → mask</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Eye protection is removed second, not first. Removing it before gloves risks transferring contamination from the glove surface to your face.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The correct doffing order is: gloves first (most contaminated), then eye protection (by ear pieces), then gown (rolled inside-out), and mask last (by ties or loops). Hand hygiene is performed after glove removal and again at the end."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct! The doffing order — gloves, eye protection, gown, mask — is designed so that each step avoids transferring contamination from outer surfaces to skin or mucous membranes. Hand hygiene follows glove removal and again after the mask."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
